sources/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-ai.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.15016) in lane agents_tools. Discovery triage only: matched=agents_tools,evaluation,inference_serving,language_models,safety_security; title_matches=agents_tools,inference_serving; score=11. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Network incident response remains slow and labor-intensive as the defender must infer multi-stage attacks from partial observations and translate recovery decisions into reliable system commands. Decision-theoretic planners provide principled optimization but typically rely on abstract states and predefined actions, while large language model (LLM) agents can reason over operational context but may hallucinate attacks and responses. Toward automating response planning, we present a hierarchical agentic response framework that integrates LLM-based attack inference, rollout planning, and digital","title":"Hierarchical Agentic Incident Response with Digital-Twin-Validated Attack Inference"}}
