rce-intake/sources/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-ai.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.15389) in lane agents_tools. Discovery triage only: matched=agents_tools,evaluation,inference_serving,language_models,safety_security,training_methods; title_matches=agents_tools,evaluation,language_models; score=14. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: LLM-based Text-to-SQL progress is reported across heterogeneous benchmarks, backbones, and inference protocols, making cross-system comparison fragile. We reframe the field as a leaderboard aggregation: we collect the metrics authors themselves report and organize them along an inference-autonomy axis spanning constrained, in-context, iterative, agentic, and reasoning-internalized generation, with traceable provenance for every cell. To anchor the aggregation empirically, we run a focused case study on Spider, comparing 8B open-source backbones with and without chain-of-thought (CoT) supervisi","title":"Agentic-SQL Revisited: Autonomy-Based Taxonomy and Empirical Benchmark Analysis for LLM Text-to-SQL"}}
