lectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-ai.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.15391) in lane agents_tools. Discovery triage only: matched=agents_tools,evaluation,language_models,safety_security; title_matches=agents_tools,language_models,safety_security; score=12. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Large language model (LLM)-assisted energy-management tools can translate natural-language context into structured grid commands, but syntactic validity does not imply physical admissibility. This paper presents TwinGridShield, a model-independent runtime authorization layer that evaluates each proposed action in a deterministic network twin before release. The prototype checks connectivity, branch-flow, generator, and load-shedding invariants and records each decision in a hash-chained log. A controlled IEEE 14-bus study evaluates single-step switching, redispatch, and load-shedding actions u","title":"TwinGridShield: Consequence-Aware Runtime Authorization for LLM Grid-Agent Actions"}}
