W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-lg.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.15567) in lane inference_serving. Discovery triage only: matched=inference_serving,language_models,memory_context,training_methods; title_matches=inference_serving,language_models; score=10. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Weight-only post-training quantization (PTQ) enables the deployment of large language models under tight memory budgets, but accuracy often collapses at 2-3 bits. Existing backpropagation-free PTQ optimizers have two limitations: group decisions ignore the correction that the remaining continuous suffix can absorb, and discrete refinements typically keep the affine quantization grid fixed. We introduce SCHUROPT, which analytically eliminates the suffix's optimal continuous response, yielding an exact groupwise quadratic with Schur-complement curvature. It then alternates closed-form row-wise s","title":"SchurQuant: Groupwise Discrete Optimization for Layer-Wise LLM Quantization"}}
{"discovery_id":"w34-event-arxiv-2608-15574","issue_id":"2026-W34","provenance":{"obligation_ids":["weekly:current-relevance","weekly:technical-significance"],"origin":"REFERENCE_EXPANSION","parent_refs":["w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-15574"],"reason":"Create one independently screenable event-level record for fresh Discovery w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-15574 by 1:1 expansion of the accepted 369-record graph; retain source identity, Raw bindings, and obligations without Screening disposition. Inventory cross-check preserves split/duplicate/chronology semantics.","research_pass":1},"schema_version":"2.0-rc1","source":{"collector_id":"arxiv-api","collector_run_id":"arxiv-api-2026-W34-20260907T161121Z","locator":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.15574","metadata":{"arxiv_id":"2608.15574","authority_class":"DISCOVERY_SOURCE_ONLY","categories":["cs.AI","cs.CV"],"chronology_precision":"EXACT_PUBLISHED_IN_ATOM_SNAPSHOT","deterministic_prefilter_hit":true,"deterministic_score":9,"discovery_only":true,"duplicate_relationship":null,"event_level_discovery_id":"w34-event-arxiv-2608-15574","event_level_expansion":true,"fresh_expansion":"w34-screening-evidence-after-sol-discovery-r2","fresh_refresh":"w34-discovery-gapfill-after-sol-review-r1","iterative_evidence_priority":true,"lane":"language_models","matched_term_groups":["evaluation","inference_serving","language_models","multimodal_media","retrieval_embeddings","safety_security","training_methods"],"primary_category":"cs.AI","provider":"arXiv","screening_decision_present":false,"selected_source_parent":"w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-15574","selection_not_performed":true,"technical_claims_accepted":false,"triage_bucket":"SEMANTIC_SHORTLIST","updated_at":"2026-08-16T06:42:11Z","window_relation_observation":"IN_WINDOW_DATE_CANDIDATE","window_utc":"[2026-08-14T22:00:00Z, 2026-08-21T22:00:00Z)"},"observed_at":"2026-09-08T00:51:52Z","published_at":"2026-08-16T06:42:11Z","raw_paths":["sources/2026-W34/execution/luna/w34-architecture-r2-research-sufficiency-revision-r1/source-intake/sources/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-ai.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.15574) in lane language_models. Discovery triage only: matched=evaluation,inference_serving,language_models,multimodal_media,retrieval_embeddings,safety_security,training_methods; title_matches=language_models; score=9. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Video question answering systems built on vision-language models often produce timestamped claims with high confidence even when unsupported by the cited frame. This deceptive hallucination arises because timestamps imply grounding without ensuring correctness, increasing user trust but not accuracy. We introduce a pipeline that closes this loop. A retrieval-augmented language model drafts answers with per-claim timestamp citations, and each cited frame is independently re-examined before being shown to the user. We compare against a plain baseline and ablate three verification designs, evalua","title":"Catching Hallucinated Citations in Video-LLM Question Answering: A Self-Verification Pipeline and Verifier Ablation Study"}}
{"discovery_id":"w34-event-arxiv-2608-15591","issue_id":"2026-W34","provenance":{"obligation_ids":["weekly:current-relevance","weekly:technical-significance"],"origin":"REFERENCE_EXPANSION","parent_refs":["w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-15591"],"reason":"Create one independently screenable event-level record for fresh Discovery w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-15591 by 1:1 expansion of the accepted 369-record graph; retain source identity, Raw bindings, and obligations without Screening disposition. Inventory cross-check preserves split/duplicate/chronology semantics.","research_pass":1},"schema_version":"2.0-rc1","source":{"collector_id":"arxiv-api","collector_run_id":"arxiv-api-2026-W34-20260907T161121Z","locator":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.15591","metadata":{"arxiv_id":"2608.15591","authority_class":"DISCOVERY_SOURCE_ONLY","categories":["cs.AI"],"chronology_precision":"EXACT_PUBLISHED_IN_ATOM_SNAPSHOT","deterministic_prefilter_hit":true,"deterministic_score":13,"discovery_only":true,"duplicate_relationship":null,"event_level_discovery_id":"w34-event-arxiv-2608-15591","event_level_expansion":true,"fresh_expansion":"w34-screening-evidence-after-sol-discovery-r2","fresh_refresh":"w34-discovery-gapfill-after-sol-review-r1","iterative_evidence_priority":true,"lane":"agents_tools","matched_term_groups":["agents_tools","evaluation","inference_serving","language_models","safety_security"],"primary_category":"cs.AI","provider":"arXiv","screening_decision_present":false,"selected_source_parent":"w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-15591","selection_not_performed":true,"technical_claims_accepted":false,"triage_bucket":"SEMANTIC_SHORTLIST","updated_at":"2026-08-16T07:27:26Z","window_relation_observation":"IN_WINDOW_DATE_CANDIDATE","window_utc":"[2026-08-14T22:00:00Z, 2026-08-21T22:00:00Z)"},"observed_at":"2026-09-08T00:51:52Z","published_at":"2026-08-16T07:27:26Z","raw_paths":["sources/2026-W34/execution/luna/w34-architecture-r2-research-sufficiency-revision-r1/source-intake/sources/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-ai.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.15591) in lane agents_tools. Discovery triage only: matched=agents_tools,evaluation,inference_serving,language_models,safety_security; title_matches=agents_tools,evaluation,language_models; score=13. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Large Language Model (LLM) agents deployed in production environments face a fundamental tension: the agent's behavior is frozen at deployment time, while the business rules and edge cases it must handle continue to evolve. Existing approaches address agent construction and one-time evaluation but provide no structured mechanism for continuous post-deployment behavioral correction without modifying the agent's source code. Most of the approaches offered in the market, require intense collection of logs and traces, and re-examining the agent design by the engineering team, a process which is he","title":"Agent Gym: A Framework for Continuous Evaluation and Evolution of LLM Agents Through Human-in-the-Loop Feedback"}}
