ns/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-lg.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.15665) in lane language_models. Discovery triage only: matched=language_models,memory_context,training_methods; title_matches=language_models,training_methods; score=9. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Zeroth-order (ZO) optimization enables backpropagation-free fine-tuning of large language models, but existing ZO methods suffer from high-variance gradient estimators, making convergence unstable and highly sensitive to learning rates. We propose SubZero+, an improved SubZero framework that improves stability in three complementary ways: (i) multi-query gradient estimation within layer-specific low-rank subspaces to reduce variance without exhibiting the multi-query paradox; (ii) a subspace Adam optimizer that performs adaptive updates using in-subspace multi-query gradient statistics; and (i","title":"SubZero+: Efficient Zeroth-Order LLM Fine-Tuning via Large Learning Rates"}}
