tors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-ai.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.15956) in lane agents_tools. Discovery triage only: matched=agents_tools,evaluation,language_models,retrieval_embeddings; title_matches=agents_tools,retrieval_embeddings; score=10. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Agentic retrieval workflows produce query, retrieval, and stopping traces as a byproduct of answering questions. We study how these traces can adapt a deployed dense retriever to changing workflow distributions without new relevance labels, synthetic queries, or LLM judgments. We introduce Navigation-Informed Embeddings (NIE), a family of trace-derived objectives. NIE-Stop turns the stopping document into a soft positive; NIE-Path additionally uses preceding path documents as hard comparisons and imposes ordinal constraints with geometric decay. A BGE encoder adapted from retained source traje","title":"Navigation-Informed Embeddings: Dense-Retriever Adaptation from Agent Search Traces"}}
{"discovery_id":"w34-event-arxiv-2608-15962","issue_id":"2026-W34","provenance":{"obligation_ids":["weekly:current-relevance","weekly:technical-significance"],"origin":"REFERENCE_EXPANSION","parent_refs":["w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-15962"],"reason":"Create one independently screenable event-level record for fresh Discovery w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-15962 by 1:1 expansion of the accepted 369-record graph; retain source identity, Raw bindings, and obligations without Screening disposition. Inventory cross-check preserves split/duplicate/chronology semantics.","research_pass":1},"schema_version":"2.0-rc1","source":{"collector_id":"arxiv-api","collector_run_id":"arxiv-api-2026-W34-20260907T161121Z","locator":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.15962","metadata":{"arxiv_id":"2608.15962","authority_class":"DISCOVERY_SOURCE_ONLY","categories":["cs.CL","cs.CV"],"chronology_precision":"EXACT_PUBLISHED_IN_ATOM_SNAPSHOT","deterministic_prefilter_hit":true,"deterministic_score":9,"discovery_only":true,"duplicate_relationship":null,"event_level_discovery_id":"w34-event-arxiv-2608-15962","event_level_expansion":true,"fresh_expansion":"w34-screening-evidence-after-sol-discovery-r2","fresh_refresh":"w34-discovery-gapfill-after-sol-review-r1","iterative_evidence_priority":true,"lane":"training_methods","matched_term_groups":["evaluation","language_models","multimodal_media","retrieval_embeddings","training_methods"],"primary_category":"cs.CL","provider":"arXiv","screening_decision_present":false,"selected_source_parent":"w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-15962","selection_not_performed":true,"technical_claims_accepted":false,"triage_bucket":"SEMANTIC_SHORTLIST","updated_at":"2026-08-16T23:30:41Z","window_relation_observation":"IN_WINDOW_DATE_CANDIDATE","window_utc":"[2026-08-14T22:00:00Z, 2026-08-21T22:00:00Z)"},"observed_at":"2026-09-08T00:51:52Z","published_at":"2026-08-16T23:30:41Z","raw_paths":["sources/2026-W34/execution/luna/w34-architecture-r2-research-sufficiency-revision-r1/source-intake/sources/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-cl.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.15962) in lane training_methods. Discovery triage only: matched=evaluation,language_models,multimodal_media,retrieval_embeddings,training_methods; title_matches=training_methods; score=9. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Long-context reasoning remains computationally expensive for large language models due to the quadratic complexity of attention over text tokens. Visual-text compression offers a promising alternative by rendering text into images and processing them with vision-language models, often reducing token usage. However, existing approaches apply uniform compression regardless of query relevance, potentially sacrificing precision where detailed extraction is required. We present SEER, a framework that learns to select query-relevant images through visual scanning and retrieve textual content only wh","title":"SEER: Long-Context Reasoning via Selective Visual-Text Compression"}}
{"discovery_id":"w34-event-arxiv-2608-15975","issue_id":"2026-W34","provenance":{"obligation_ids":["weekly:current-relevance","weekly:technical-significance"],"origin":"REFERENCE_EXPANSION","parent_refs":["w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-15975"],"reason":"Create one independently screenable event-level record for fresh Discovery w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-15975 by 1:1 expansion of the accepted 369-record graph; retain source identity, Raw bindings, and obligations without Screening disposition. Inventory cross-check preserves split/duplicate/chronology semantics.","research_pass":1},"schema_version":"2.0-rc1","source":{"collector_id":"arxiv-api","collector_run_id":"arxiv-api-2026-W34-20260907T161121Z","locator":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.15975","metadata":{"arxiv_id":"2608.15975","authority_class":"DISCOVERY_SOURCE_ONLY","categories":["cs.AI","cs.CL","cs.DC","cs.LG"],"chronology_precision":"EXACT_PUBLISHED_IN_ATOM_SNAPSHOT","deterministic_prefilter_hit":true,"deterministic_score":12,"discovery_only":true,"duplicate_relationship":null,"event_level_discovery_id":"w34-event-arxiv-2608-15975","event_level_expansion":true,"fresh_expansion":"w34-screening-evidence-after-sol-discovery-r2","fresh_refresh":"w34-discovery-gapfill-after-sol-review-r1","iterative_evidence_priority":true,"lane":"language_models","matched_term_groups":["evaluation","language_models","memory_context","training_methods"],"primary_category":"cs.AI","provider":"arXiv","screening_decision_present":false,"selected_source_parent":"w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-15975","selection_not_performed":true,"technical_claims_accepted":false,"triage_bucket":"SEMANTIC_SHORTLIST","updated_at":"2026-08-17T00:02:25Z","window_relation_observation":"IN_WINDOW_DATE_CANDIDATE","window_utc":"[2026-08-14T22:00:00Z, 2026-08-21T22:00:00Z)"},"observed_at":"2026-09-08T00:51:52Z","published_at":"2026-08-17T00:02:25Z","raw_paths":["sources/2026-W34/execution/luna/w34-architecture-r2-research-sufficiency-revision-r1/source-intake/sources/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-ai.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.15975) in lane language_models. Discovery triage only: matched=evaluation,language_models,memory_context,training_methods; title_matches=language_models,memory_context,training_methods; score=12. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Labeling large text corpora with LLM teachers has become a practical route to training data at scale. At millions of items, hand-labeling every batch is not feasible, and two questions dominate: what label quality a teacher buys per dollar, and how to keep a fleet of GPU workers busy under skewed, failure-prone workloads. We present a simple, reproducible pipeline that addresses both. First, a work-stealing ring pool: each worker owns a queue, drains it first, and then steals from ring successors, with exactly-once task claims via atomic conditional writes and crash tolerance via stale-claim s","title":"A Scalable Pipeline for LLM-Teacher Distillation Labeling: Work-Stealing Job Scheduling and Memory-Aware GPU Concurrency"}}
{"discovery_id":"w34-event-arxiv-2608-16002","issue_id":"2026-W34","provenance":{"obligation_ids":["weekly:current-relevance","weekly:technical-significance"],"origin":"REFERENCE_EXPANSION","parent_refs":["w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-16002"],"reason":"Create one independently screenable event-level record for fresh Discovery w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-16002 by 1:1 expansion of the accepted 369-record graph; retain source identity, Raw bindings, and obligations without Screening disposition. Inventory cross-check preserves split/duplicate/chronology semantics.","research_pass":1},"schema_version":"2.0-rc1","source":{"collector_id":"arxiv-api","collector_run_id":"arxiv-api-2026-W34-20260907T161121Z","locator":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.16002","metadata":{"arxiv_id":"2608.16002","authority_class":"DISCOVERY_SOURCE_ONLY","categories":["cs.AI","cs.CL"],"chronology_precision":"EXACT_PUBLISHED_IN_ATOM_SNAPSHOT","deterministic_prefilter_hit":true,"deterministic_score":9,"discovery_only":true,"duplicate_relationship":null,"event_level_discovery_id":"w34-event-arxiv-2608-16002","event_level_expansion":true,"fresh_expansion":"w34-screening-evidence-after-sol-discovery-r2","fresh_refresh":"w34-discovery-gapfill-after-sol-review-r1","iterative_evidence_priority":true,"lane":"agents_tools","matched_term_groups":["agents_tools","evaluation","language_models","safety_security","training_methods"],"primary_category":"cs.AI","provider":"arXiv","screening_decision_present":false,"selected_source_parent":"w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-16002","selection_not_performed":true,"technical_claims_accepted":false,"triage_bucket":"SEMANTIC_SHORTLIST","updated_at":"2026-08-19T01:59:37Z","window_relation_observation":"IN_WINDOW_DATE_CANDIDATE","window_utc":"[2026-08-14T22:00:00Z, 2026-08-21T22:00:00Z)"},"observed_at":"2026-09-08T00:51:52Z","published_at":"2026-08-17T01:40:14Z","raw_paths":["sources/2026-W34/execution/luna/w34-architecture-r2-research-sufficiency-revision-r1/source-intake/sources/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-ai.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.16002) in lane agents_tools. Discovery triage only: matched=agents_tools,evaluation,language_models,safety_security,training_methods; title_matches=agents_tools,language_models; score=9. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Reliable uncertainty quantification (UQ) is essential for deploying large language model (LLM) agents in complex interactive environments. Existing UQ methods largely rely on local signals, such as token probabilities, predictive entropy, or per-step confidence, and therefore overlook the long-range dependencies through which errors accumulate across an execution trajectory. As a result, they may fail to identify agent failures whose causes originate several reasoning or interaction steps before the final answer. We propose RUPA (Relational Uncertainty Propagation for Agents), a trajectory-lev","title":"From Sequence to Structure: Relational Uncertainty Propagation for LLM Agents"}}
