/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-cr.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.16026) in lane inference_serving. Discovery triage only: matched=agents_tools,inference_serving,language_models,safety_security; title_matches=inference_serving,safety_security; score=10. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Skills for large language model (LLM) agents have been widely deployed across diverse application domains. However, we observe that these skills generate specific traffic patterns during execution. In this paper, we design a pipeline that generates specific traffic patterns by inserting carefully designed skill descriptions, which we term skill watermarks, so that a passive network attacker can establish a covert channel to encode private information within observable traffic across multiple conversation turns. Specifically, we insert prompt constraint terms, referred to as watermarks, into th","title":"SkillWatermark: An Embedded Skill Watermark of Progressive Privacy Inference via Benign Prompts"}}
