e-intake/sources/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-ai.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.16402) in lane agents_tools. Discovery triage only: matched=agents_tools,evaluation,inference_serving,language_models,memory_context,safety_security; title_matches=agents_tools,inference_serving; score=10. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Large language model-based agentic frameworks primarily optimize capability: whether an agent can reason, retrieve information, call tools, delegate work, and complete a goal. Enterprise execution requires a stronger property. A successful result is not reliable if it was produced through unauthorized data access, widened delegated authority, unapproved side effects, unrecoverable budget consumption, or incomplete evidence. This paper defines reliable capability as a path property: an agent is reliably capable only when it completes a task through action events that remain admissible under ide","title":"A Policy Algebra for Trust-Preserving Agentic AI Execution"}}
