take/sources/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-ai.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.16411) in lane agents_tools. Discovery triage only: matched=agents_tools,developer_systems,language_models,safety_security,training_methods; title_matches=agents_tools; score=9. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: LLM-based agents are rapidly moving from research prototypes into the core business processes of organizations, but these agents pose deployment risks to security, compliance, and functionality. In this article, we argue that risk-free deployment must be grounded in the agent's trajectory: the recorded sequence of reasoning steps, tool invocations, and environmental observations. Trajectories are available for any agent, and many failures are visible only in the trajectory. To make agents deployable and sustainable, we advocate agent testing and debugging as a systematic research direction for","title":"Towards Risk-free AI Agent Deployment"}}
