/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-cr.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.16422) in lane language_models. Discovery triage only: matched=agents_tools,evaluation,language_models,safety_security,training_methods; title_matches=language_models,safety_security; score=9. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Cyber threats continue to escalate in both frequency and sophistication, necessitating more adaptive and scalable defense strategies. This paper explores how Large Language Models (LLMs) can bolster cybersecurity simulations by automating the creation of synthetic environments and identifying latent vulnerabilities. We employ YAML as a structured representation format for simulating complex network configurations, thereby enabling Large Language Model-driven pipelines to support and improve reinforcement learning (RL) agent training. Comparative studies examine the advantages of LLM-based tech","title":"Proving the Utility of Large Language Models in Cybersecurity Simulations: A Comprehensive Examination"}}
