ficiency-revision-r1/source-intake/sources/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-cv.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.16721) in lane agents_tools. Discovery triage only: matched=agents_tools,evaluation,inference_serving,multimodal_media,retrieval_embeddings,safety_security,training_methods; title_matches=agents_tools,multimodal_media; score=11. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: The rapid evolution of text-to-image (T2I) generation models has effectively solved the foundational challenge of raw pixel synthesis, shifting the community's focus toward fulfilling increasingly intricate user requests. While recent agentic image generation workflows enhance static inference with advanced capabilities like external knowledge retrieval and iterative reasoning, they mostly operate in isolated silos with fixed ``one-size-fits-all\" topologies. This inevitably leads to severe compute-mismatch, where simple queries are forced through computationally heavy pipelines. To bridge this","title":"GenRouter: Unified Workflow Routing for Agentic Image Generation"}}
