rces/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-cl.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.17184) in lane safety_security. Discovery triage only: matched=agents_tools,evaluation,language_models,retrieval_embeddings,safety_security; title_matches=safety_security; score=9. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Job Safety Analysis (JSA) and pre-task planning can benefit from prior incident records, yet historical accident data is often stored as unstructured narratives that are difficult to consult at the point of planning. A novel framework centered on large language models (LLMs) for highway construction safety reporting and planning is proposed as a foundation for future agentic applications, prioritizing deterministic, local inferencing. The first aim is to enable classification and quality scoring of incident narratives for existing and future reporting purposes. The second is to evaluate retrie","title":"AISA: AI Safety Assistant Framework for Continuous Improvement of Highway Construction"}}
