rces/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-cv.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.17723) in lane language_models. Discovery triage only: matched=evaluation,language_models,multimodal_media,safety_security,training_methods; title_matches=language_models,multimodal_media; score=9. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Analog gauges remain common in industrial environments where manual inspection is costly or hazardous. The engineering application addressed here is direct numerical reading of single-target analog-gauge images, while the artificial-intelligence contribution is a systematic evaluation of specialization, transfer, robustness and reliability for a general-purpose vision-language model (VLM) without an explicit pointer-segmentation and geometric-reading pipeline. The Qwen2.5-VL-7B-Instruct model is evaluated using zero-shot prompting, in-context learning (ICL) and parameter-efficient fine-tuning","title":"Vision-Language Models for Analog Gauge Reading: An Empirical Study of Specialization, Transfer and Reliability"}}
{"discovery_id":"w34-event-arxiv-2608-17756","issue_id":"2026-W34","provenance":{"obligation_ids":["weekly:current-relevance","weekly:technical-significance"],"origin":"REFERENCE_EXPANSION","parent_refs":["w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-17756"],"reason":"Create one independently screenable event-level record for fresh Discovery w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-17756 by 1:1 expansion of the accepted 369-record graph; retain source identity, Raw bindings, and obligations without Screening disposition. Inventory cross-check preserves split/duplicate/chronology semantics.","research_pass":1},"schema_version":"2.0-rc1","source":{"collector_id":"arxiv-api","collector_run_id":"arxiv-api-2026-W34-20260907T161121Z","locator":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.17756","metadata":{"arxiv_id":"2608.17756","authority_class":"DISCOVERY_SOURCE_ONLY","categories":["cs.AI"],"chronology_precision":"EXACT_PUBLISHED_IN_ATOM_SNAPSHOT","deterministic_prefilter_hit":true,"deterministic_score":14,"discovery_only":true,"duplicate_relationship":null,"event_level_discovery_id":"w34-event-arxiv-2608-17756","event_level_expansion":true,"fresh_expansion":"w34-screening-evidence-after-sol-discovery-r2","fresh_refresh":"w34-discovery-gapfill-after-sol-review-r1","iterative_evidence_priority":true,"lane":"agents_tools","matched_term_groups":["agents_tools","evaluation","inference_serving","language_models","memory_context","retrieval_embeddings"],"primary_category":"cs.AI","provider":"arXiv","screening_decision_present":false,"selected_source_parent":"w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-17756","selection_not_performed":true,"technical_claims_accepted":false,"triage_bucket":"SEMANTIC_SHORTLIST","updated_at":"2026-08-19T02:59:03Z","window_relation_observation":"IN_WINDOW_DATE_CANDIDATE","window_utc":"[2026-08-14T22:00:00Z, 2026-08-21T22:00:00Z)"},"observed_at":"2026-09-08T00:51:52Z","published_at":"2026-08-18T13:18:38Z","raw_paths":["sources/2026-W34/execution/luna/w34-architecture-r2-research-sufficiency-revision-r1/source-intake/sources/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-ai.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.17756) in lane agents_tools. Discovery triage only: matched=agents_tools,evaluation,inference_serving,language_models,memory_context,retrieval_embeddings; title_matches=agents_tools,inference_serving,memory_context; score=14. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Memory is a key capability of LLM agents. Persistent memory extends this across sessions---enabling recall, revision, and personalization. Yet its multi-stage pipeline (ingestion, retrieval, filtering, generation) makes failures difficult to localize: end-to-end evaluation reveals that an error occurred, but not which stage caused it. Existing evaluations often report aggregate performance without paired statistical comparisons, slice-level non-regression checks, or stage-level diagnostic traces. We propose D$^2$ACCI (Diagnostic-Driven Artifact-based Closed-loop Controlled Iteration), a dual-l","title":"D$^2$ACCI: A Dual-Loop Diagnostic Protocol for Evidence-Preserving Agent Memory"}}
