es/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-ai.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.17889) in lane agents_tools. Discovery triage only: matched=agents_tools,evaluation,inference_serving,retrieval_embeddings; title_matches=agents_tools,evaluation,retrieval_embeddings; score=12. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Visually rich documents encode relevance through language, layout, structured visual elements, and corpus context, yet retrieval is typically evaluated by one-shot query--page matching. Agentic-search benchmarks usually score downstream question answering or report generation, leaving document ranking under iterative evidence acquisition underexplored. We introduce VisDocAgentBench, a closed-corpus benchmark comparing static and agentic retrieval under a shared ranked-output contract. It contains 2,375 pages from 100 documents and 120 unique-target queries balanced across direct, one-bridge, a","title":"VisDocAgentBench: Benchmarking Agents for Visually Rich Document Retrieval"}}
