collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-ai.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.17895) in lane evaluation. Discovery triage only: matched=evaluation,language_models,multimodal_media,training_methods; title_matches=evaluation,multimodal_media,training_methods; score=12. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: While Multimodal Large Language Models (MLLMs) have made significant strides in visual comprehension, their ability to reason about text-dense, professional documents remains incompletely evaluated. Existing benchmarks emphasize information extraction, require external domain knowledge, or cover professional documents only as one of many settings. They are also largely English- or Chinese-centric, leaving other languages and Russian, in particular, substantially underrepresented. To address these limitations, we introduce BEAR-Bench (Bilingual Enterprise and Academic Reasoning), a self-contain","title":"BEAR-Bench: A Bilingual Enterprise and Academic Reasoning Benchmark for Multimodal Models"}}
