ollectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-ai.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.18586) in lane evaluation. Discovery triage only: matched=evaluation,language_models,multimodal_media,safety_security; title_matches=evaluation,multimodal_media; score=10. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Multimodal large language models (MLLMs) are increasingly used as OCR systems in document and knowledge-processing pipelines, but their ability to faithfully read real handwriting remains underexplored. Existing OCR benchmarks focus largely on printed text or clean single-line inputs, leaving limited coverage of realistic handwritten OCR scenarios such as multilingual handwriting, writer errors, and structurally complex mathematical expressions. We introduce OmniHandwritingOCR, a diagnostic benchmark for evaluating MLLMs and OCR systems on handwritten OCR. It covers handwritten text recognitio","title":"OmniHandwritingOCR: A Diagnostic Benchmark for Evaluating Multimodal LLMs in Handwritten OCR Scenarios"}}
{"discovery_id":"w34-event-arxiv-2608-18591","issue_id":"2026-W34","provenance":{"obligation_ids":["weekly:current-relevance","weekly:technical-significance"],"origin":"REFERENCE_EXPANSION","parent_refs":["w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-18591"],"reason":"Create one independently screenable event-level record for fresh Discovery w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-18591 by 1:1 expansion of the accepted 369-record graph; retain source identity, Raw bindings, and obligations without Screening disposition. Inventory cross-check preserves split/duplicate/chronology semantics.","research_pass":1},"schema_version":"2.0-rc1","source":{"collector_id":"arxiv-api","collector_run_id":"arxiv-api-2026-W34-20260907T161121Z","locator":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.18591","metadata":{"arxiv_id":"2608.18591","authority_class":"DISCOVERY_SOURCE_ONLY","categories":["cs.AI","cs.CL"],"chronology_precision":"EXACT_PUBLISHED_IN_ATOM_SNAPSHOT","deterministic_prefilter_hit":true,"deterministic_score":15,"discovery_only":true,"duplicate_relationship":null,"event_level_discovery_id":"w34-event-arxiv-2608-18591","event_level_expansion":true,"fresh_expansion":"w34-screening-evidence-after-sol-discovery-r2","fresh_refresh":"w34-discovery-gapfill-after-sol-review-r1","iterative_evidence_priority":true,"lane":"inference_serving","matched_term_groups":["evaluation","inference_serving","language_models","multimodal_media","training_methods"],"primary_category":"cs.AI","provider":"arXiv","screening_decision_present":false,"selected_source_parent":"w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-18591","selection_not_performed":true,"technical_claims_accepted":false,"triage_bucket":"SEMANTIC_SHORTLIST","updated_at":"2026-08-19T06:33:33Z","window_relation_observation":"IN_WINDOW_DATE_CANDIDATE","window_utc":"[2026-08-14T22:00:00Z, 2026-08-21T22:00:00Z)"},"observed_at":"2026-09-08T00:51:52Z","published_at":"2026-08-19T06:33:33Z","raw_paths":["sources/2026-W34/execution/luna/w34-architecture-r2-research-sufficiency-revision-r1/source-intake/sources/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-ai.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.18591) in lane inference_serving. Discovery triage only: matched=evaluation,inference_serving,language_models,multimodal_media,training_methods; title_matches=inference_serving,language_models,multimodal_media,training_methods; score=15. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Uniformly allocating inference reasoning budgets to LLMs is expensive and prone to over-thinking penalties; especially in document tasks where visual layouts drive complexity. To address this, we introduce BudgetDoc, the first multimodal benchmark providing explicit supervision for model-budget-performance trade-offs across three document tasks. Using BudgetDoc, we train DRB (Document-Reasoning Balancer), an approx. 1B-parameter pre-flight estimator (SigLIP-2 + Qwen3-0.6B) that predicts ordinal model performance across budget levels, achieving a 0.753 weighted F1. When dynamically allocating r","title":"Can a Lightweight Multimodal Model Estimate LLM Reasoning Performance? A Study for Compute-Optimal Document Inference"}}
{"discovery_id":"w34-event-arxiv-2608-18613","issue_id":"2026-W34","provenance":{"obligation_ids":["weekly:current-relevance","weekly:technical-significance"],"origin":"REFERENCE_EXPANSION","parent_refs":["w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-18613"],"reason":"Create one independently screenable event-level record for fresh Discovery w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-18613 by 1:1 expansion of the accepted 369-record graph; retain source identity, Raw bindings, and obligations without Screening disposition. Inventory cross-check preserves split/duplicate/chronology semantics.","research_pass":1},"schema_version":"2.0-rc1","source":{"collector_id":"arxiv-api","collector_run_id":"arxiv-api-2026-W34-20260907T161121Z","locator":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.18613","metadata":{"arxiv_id":"2608.18613","authority_class":"DISCOVERY_SOURCE_ONLY","categories":["cs.AI","cs.CR"],"chronology_precision":"EXACT_PUBLISHED_IN_ATOM_SNAPSHOT","deterministic_prefilter_hit":true,"deterministic_score":12,"discovery_only":true,"duplicate_relationship":null,"event_level_discovery_id":"w34-event-arxiv-2608-18613","event_level_expansion":true,"fresh_expansion":"w34-screening-evidence-after-sol-discovery-r2","fresh_refresh":"w34-discovery-gapfill-after-sol-review-r1","iterative_evidence_priority":true,"lane":"agents_tools","matched_term_groups":["agents_tools","evaluation","language_models","memory_context","retrieval_embeddings","safety_security"],"primary_category":"cs.AI","provider":"arXiv","screening_decision_present":false,"selected_source_parent":"w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-18613","selection_not_performed":true,"technical_claims_accepted":false,"triage_bucket":"SEMANTIC_SHORTLIST","updated_at":"2026-08-19T07:00:29Z","window_relation_observation":"IN_WINDOW_DATE_CANDIDATE","window_utc":"[2026-08-14T22:00:00Z, 2026-08-21T22:00:00Z)"},"observed_at":"2026-09-08T00:51:52Z","published_at":"2026-08-19T07:00:29Z","raw_paths":["sources/2026-W34/execution/luna/w34-architecture-r2-research-sufficiency-revision-r1/source-intake/sources/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-ai.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.18613) in lane agents_tools. Discovery triage only: matched=agents_tools,evaluation,language_models,memory_context,retrieval_embeddings,safety_security; title_matches=agents_tools,safety_security; score=12. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Cyber threat intelligence (CTI) is increasingly consumed not by human analysts but by LLM agents that compose multi-step investigations at query time. The harness side of this shift has matured rapidly (planning loops, tool protocols, context management), but the corpus side has not: threat reports and vulnerability databases are still packaged for retrieval-augmented generation, as opaque chunks behind an embedding index. We argue that this substrate, not model capability, is the bottleneck on agentic CTI investigation, and present CTIFoundry, an agent-native corpus scaffold. At build time, C","title":"CTIFoundry: An Agent-Native Corpus Scaffold for Cyber Threat Intelligence"}}
{"discovery_id":"w34-event-arxiv-2608-18628","issue_id":"2026-W34","provenance":{"obligation_ids":["weekly:current-relevance","weekly:technical-significance"],"origin":"REFERENCE_EXPANSION","parent_refs":["w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-18628"],"reason":"Create one independently screenable event-level record for fresh Discovery w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-18628 by 1:1 expansion of the accepted 369-record graph; retain source identity, Raw bindings, and obligations without Screening disposition. Inventory cross-check preserves split/duplicate/chronology semantics.","research_pass":1},"schema_version":"2.0-rc1","source":{"collector_id":"arxiv-api","collector_run_id":"arxiv-api-2026-W34-20260907T161121Z","locator":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.18628","metadata":{"arxiv_id":"2608.18628","authority_class":"DISCOVERY_SOURCE_ONLY","categories":["cs.CL","cs.CV"],"chronology_precision":"EXACT_PUBLISHED_IN_ATOM_SNAPSHOT","deterministic_prefilter_hit":true,"deterministic_score":13,"discovery_only":true,"duplicate_relationship":null,"event_level_discovery_id":"w34-event-arxiv-2608-18628","event_level_expansion":true,"fresh_expansion":"w34-screening-evidence-after-sol-discovery-r2","fresh_refresh":"w34-discovery-gapfill-after-sol-review-r1","iterative_evidence_priority":true,"lane":"language_models","matched_term_groups":["evaluation","language_models","multimodal_media","safety_security","training_methods"],"primary_category":"cs.CL","provider":"arXiv","screening_decision_present":false,"selected_source_parent":"w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-18628","selection_not_performed":true,"technical_claims_accepted":false,"triage_bucket":"SEMANTIC_SHORTLIST","updated_at":"2026-08-19T07:22:15Z","window_relation_observation":"IN_WINDOW_DATE_CANDIDATE","window_utc":"[2026-08-14T22:00:00Z, 2026-08-21T22:00:00Z)"},"observed_at":"2026-09-08T00:51:52Z","published_at":"2026-08-19T07:22:15Z","raw_paths":["sources/2026-W34/execution/luna/w34-architecture-r2-research-sufficiency-revision-r1/source-intake/sources/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-cl.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.18628) in lane language_models. Discovery triage only: matched=evaluation,language_models,multimodal_media,safety_security,training_methods; title_matches=language_models,multimodal_media,safety_security; score=13. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Aligned vision-language models (VLMs) are designed to balance grounded visual reasoning with safe generation behavior. However, we observe a striking phenomenon: under safety-constrained instruction, models frequently abstain from answering questions that remain correctly answerable under default instruction despite receiving identical image-question inputs. This raises a fundamental question: does safety alignment suppress perceptual grounding itself, or does visual evidence remain internally available while generation is redirected toward abstention? In this work, we investigate the internal","title":"When Safety Overrides Vision: Exploring Dynamics between Vision Influence and Safety Alignment in Vision-Language Models"}}
{"discovery_id":"w34-event-arxiv-2608-18631","issue_id":"2026-W34","provenance":{"obligation_ids":["weekly:current-relevance","weekly:technical-significance"],"origin":"REFERENCE_EXPANSION","parent_refs":["w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-18631"],"reason":"Create one independently screenable event-level record for fresh Discovery w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-18631 by 1:1 expansion of the accepted 369-record graph; retain source identity, Raw bindings, and obligations without Screening disposition. Inventory cross-check preserves split/duplicate/chronology semantics.","research_pass":1},"schema_version":"2.0-rc1","source":{"collector_id":"arxiv-api","collector_run_id":"arxiv-api-2026-W34-20260907T161121Z","locator":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.18631","metadata":{"arxiv_id":"2608.18631","authority_class":"DISCOVERY_SOURCE_ONLY","categories":["cs.AI","cs.GT","cs.LG"],"chronology_precision":"EXACT_PUBLISHED_IN_ATOM_SNAPSHOT","deterministic_prefilter_hit":true,"deterministic_score":11,"discovery_only":true,"duplicate_relationship":null,"event_level_discovery_id":"w34-event-arxiv-2608-18631","event_level_expansion":true,"fresh_expansion":"w34-screening-evidence-after-sol-discovery-r2","fresh_refresh":"w34-discovery-gapfill-after-sol-review-r1","iterative_evidence_priority":true,"lane":"language_models","matched_term_groups":["agents_tools","evaluation","language_models","safety_security","training_methods"],"primary_category":"cs.AI","provider":"arXiv","screening_decision_present":false,"selected_source_parent":"w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-18631","selection_not_performed":true,"technical_claims_accepted":false,"triage_bucket":"SEMANTIC_SHORTLIST","updated_at":"2026-08-19T07:27:12Z","window_relation_observation":"IN_WINDOW_DATE_CANDIDATE","window_utc":"[2026-08-14T22:00:00Z, 2026-08-21T22:00:00Z)"},"observed_at":"2026-09-08T00:51:52Z","published_at":"2026-08-19T07:27:12Z","raw_paths":["sources/2026-W34/execution/luna/w34-architecture-r2-research-sufficiency-revision-r1/source-intake/sources/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-ai.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.18631) in lane language_models. Discovery triage only: matched=agents_tools,evaluation,language_models,safety_security,training_methods; title_matches=language_models,training_methods; score=11. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: As large language models evolve into decision-making agents, the ability to reason over preferences becomes fundamental to alignment, coordination, and collective intelligence. Yet, unlike standard benchmarks, real-world preference reasoning is inherently indeterminate: information may be incomplete, and valid solutions may not exist. We argue that indeterminacy, rather than correctness alone, is a central challenge for AI reasoning. We formalize this challenge along two axes, (i) epistemic indeterminacy, arising from incomplete, partial, or expressive preferences, and (ii) structural indeterm","title":"Preference Reasoning under Indeterminacy in Large Language Models"}}
{"discovery_id":"w34-event-arxiv-2608-18640","issue_id":"2026-W34","provenance":{"obligation_ids":["weekly:current-relevance","weekly:technical-significance"],"origin":"REFERENCE_EXPANSION","parent_refs":["w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-18640"],"reason":"Create one independently screenable event-level record for fresh Discovery w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-18640 by 1:1 expansion of the accepted 369-record graph; retain source identity, Raw bindings, and obligations without Screening disposition. Inventory cross-check preserves split/duplicate/chronology semantics.","research_pass":1},"schema_version":"2.0-rc1","source":{"collector_id":"arxiv-api","collector_run_id":"arxiv-api-2026-W34-20260907T161121Z","locator":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.18640","metadata":{"arxiv_id":"2608.18640","authority_class":"DISCOVERY_SOURCE_ONLY","categories":["cs.CV"],"chronology_precision":"EXACT_PUBLISHED_IN_ATOM_SNAPSHOT","deterministic_prefilter_hit":true,"deterministic_score":9,"discovery_only":true,"duplicate_relationship":null,"event_level_discovery_id":"w34-event-arxiv-2608-18640","event_level_expansion":true,"fresh_expansion":"w34-screening-evidence-after-sol-discovery-r2","fresh_refresh":"w34-discovery-gapfill-after-sol-review-r1","iterative_evidence_priority":true,"lane":"memory_context","matched_term_groups":["evaluation","inference_serving","memory_context","retrieval_embeddings","safety_security"],"primary_category":"cs.CV","provider":"arXiv","screening_decision_present":false,"selected_source_parent":"w34-gapfill-arxiv-triage-2608-18640","selection_not_performed":true,"technical_claims_accepted":false,"triage_bucket":"SEMANTIC_SHORTLIST","updated_at":"2026-08-19T07:40:39Z","window_relation_observation":"IN_WINDOW_DATE_CANDIDATE","window_utc":"[2026-08-14T22:00:00Z, 2026-08-21T22:00:00Z)"},"observed_at":"2026-09-08T00:51:52Z","published_at":"2026-08-19T07:40:39Z","raw_paths":["sources/2026-W34/execution/luna/w34-architecture-r2-research-sufficiency-revision-r1/source-intake/sources/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-cv.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.18640) in lane memory_context. Discovery triage only: matched=evaluation,inference_serving,memory_context,retrieval_embeddings,safety_security; title_matches=memory_context; score=9. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Long-term video object segmentation (VOS) remains challenging due to error accumulation under extended occlusions, re-appearance, and scene changes. Although SAM2 provides strong zero-shot performance, its streaming memory can amplify drift over long horizons when recent, unreliable predictions dominate the memory state. We propose SAM2Dual, a training-free, plug-and-play inference-time enhancement that improves long-video robustness without updating model weights. SAM2Dual introduces a Dual Memory design that explicitly separates (i) short-term memory for rapid local adaptation and (ii) long-","title":"SAM2Dual: Training-Free, Dual Memory for Long-Term Video Object Segmentation"}}
