n-r1/source-intake/sources/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-cv.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.18734) in lane multimodal_media. Discovery triage only: matched=agents_tools,evaluation,language_models,multimodal_media,retrieval_embeddings,training_methods; title_matches=multimodal_media,training_methods; score=12. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: 4D understanding and reasoning is a fundamental capability for embodied AI agents operating in dynamic physical environments. However, existing vision encoders are largely limited to static 2D images or 3D point clouds without temporal modeling, or to 2D videos that lack accurate geometric depth reasoning. Consequently, current approaches fail to jointly capture spatial structure and motion evolution in dynamic scenes. We present CL4D, the first foundational 4D vision encoder that directly operates on dynamic point clouds, trained with a contrastive learning objective to align spatio-temporal","title":"CL4D: Contrastive Language-4D Pretraining for Vision-Language Reasoning in Dynamic Scenes"}}
