ce-intake/sources/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-lg.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.19297) in lane evaluation. Discovery triage only: matched=evaluation,language_models,memory_context,multimodal_media,safety_security,training_methods; title_matches=evaluation,memory_context,multimodal_media; score=14. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: While multimodal large language models (MLLMs) excel in medical applications, most of them favor static images or short-term signals. In the critical field of dynamic electrocardiograms (ECG), models struggle with complex temporal reasoning and diagnostic report generation due to a lack of high-quality datasets and benchmarks. To address this, we introduce (i) Holtercare-23K, a large-scale multimodal dynamic ECG dataset comprising 22,980 QA pairs derived from 788 clinical Holter records and featuring a novel signal-video-text tri-modal alignment. Based on this dataset, we present (ii) Holterca","title":"Holtercare-Bench: A Multimodal Benchmark for Evaluating Long-Term Dynamic ECG Analysis"}}
