take/sources/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-ai.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.19800) in lane safety_security. Discovery triage only: matched=evaluation,inference_serving,memory_context,safety_security,training_methods; title_matches=safety_security; score=9. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Low-Rank Adaptation (LoRA) is a prominent fine-tuning method for large models, achieving competitive performance with reduced memory overhead. However, a persistent performance gap remains between LoRA and full fine-tuning. Recent studies have sought to narrow this gap by employing one-step gradient approximations of pretrained weights to align LoRA updates with the principal directions or intrinsic dimensionalities of full fine-tuning updates. Nevertheless, these approaches fail to capture the full dynamics of the gradients. In this paper, we propose LoRA-GA$^2$, an effective fine-tuning algo","title":"LoRA-GA$^2$: Low Rank Adaptation with Multi-step Gradient Adaptive Alignment"}}
