20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-ai.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.19901) in lane agents_tools. Discovery triage only: matched=agents_tools,evaluation,language_models; title_matches=agents_tools,evaluation; score=9. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Agent Skills extend LLM agents with reusable instruction packages that may also include scripts, resources, and service configuration. This creates a direct distribution channel for malicious behavior, yet existing malicious-Skill datasets are fragmented across sources, artifact formats, evidence regimes, and benign coverage; duplicated and structurally related content further complicates direct aggregation and evaluation. We present MaliciousSkillBench, a comprehensive benchmark for malicious Agent Skill detection. We consolidate 13 public sources, 11 of which contribute Core malicious artifa","title":"MaliciousSkillBench: A Comprehensive Benchmark for Malicious Agent Skill Detection"}}
