2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-lg.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.20024) in lane evaluation. Discovery triage only: matched=evaluation,inference_serving,language_models,memory_context,training_methods; title_matches=evaluation; score=9. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: District heating energy hubs require reliable heat load forecasts for efficient operational scheduling. Conventional forecasting workflows train system-specific models on historical data, which can become burdensome when networks change through new consumers, retrofits, or changing operating regimes. Zero-shot time-series foundation models and in-context forecasting offer a promising alternative: they can adapt at inference time from recent observations rather than by repeated retraining. This study systematically evaluates TabPFN-TS against time-series foundation models and trained machine-le","title":"Systematic Evaluation of TabPFN-TS for Zero-Shot Probabilistic Heat Load Forecasting in District Heating Networks"}}
