ectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-lg.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.20123) in lane inference_serving. Discovery triage only: matched=inference_serving,language_models,training_methods; title_matches=inference_serving,training_methods; score=9. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: We study inference-time control for text generation in discrete diffusion language models, where the goal is to steer sampling toward sequence-level rewards without retraining. Prior work in this domain has focused on particle-based methods such as best-of-$n$ sampling and bootstrap sequential Monte Carlo, which may suffer from overoptimism and weight degeneracy, respectively. We address these limitations using \\emph{nested} sequential Monte Carlo methods. We formulate nested SMC (NSMC) and fully-adapted nested SMC (FA-NSMC) for Feynman--Kac steering, identifying and correcting errors in prior","title":"Discrete Diffusion Inference-Time Control with Nested Sequential Monte Carlo"}}
