ource-intake/sources/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-cl.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.20129) in lane agents_tools. Discovery triage only: matched=agents_tools,language_models,multimodal_media,safety_security,training_methods; title_matches=agents_tools,training_methods; score=11. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Autonomous vehicles require robust perception and decision-making capabilities to operate in diverse and unseen scenarios. While reinforcement learning and rule-based methods can provide effective control and safety mechanisms, their performance may degrade in situations requiring contextual reasoning. Large Language Models (LLMs) have demonstrated strong capabilities in understanding multimodal information and generating contextual reasoning, however, their use for direct vehicle control can introduce latency and hallucination risks. To address these limitations, a hybrid framework is propose","title":"Multi-Agent Orchestration with the Common-Sense Reasoning Capabilities of LLMs for Autonomous Driving"}}
