ources/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-cv.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.20720) in lane multimodal_media. Discovery triage only: matched=evaluation,language_models,multimodal_media,safety_security,training_methods; title_matches=multimodal_media,training_methods; score=11. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Open-world 3D affordance grounding requires localizing functional object parts in 3D given free-form language queries. Existing methods typically assume pre-built object-centric 3D geometry and closed affordance ontologies, limiting deployment from raw RGB observations. We present AffordAny, an end-to-end framework that uses one monocular RGB image to construct large-scale text-conditioned 3D part supervision, ground affordances with a frozen vision-language model (VLM) guided decoder, and improve open-world generalization through pseudo-label self-training. Our automated pipeline produces a b","title":"AffordAny: Open-World 3D Affordance Grounding from Monocular RGB Images via Vision-Language-Guided Geometric Reasoning"}}
