collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-cl.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.21030) in lane language_models. Discovery triage only: matched=language_models,multimodal_media,training_methods; title_matches=language_models,multimodal_media,training_methods; score=11. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Video multimodal large language models have advanced significantly, yet fine-grained motion-temporal understanding remains fragile. The core bottleneck is not only sparse frame sampling, but also the lack of a complete temporal modeling pipeline for explicitly representing frame-to-frame change, enabling appearance-motion interaction, and optimizing temporal direction sensitivity. We propose COMET, a temporally grounded framework that systematically strengthens video MLLMs through explicit temporal representation, appearance-motion fusion, and direction-aware optimization. Architecturally, COM","title":"COMET: Contrastive Motion-Enhanced Temporal Reasoning for Video Multimodal Large Language Models"}}
