s/2026-W34/collectors/arxiv/runs/20260907T161121Z/raw/cs-ai.atom"],"source_type":"arxiv_atom_snapshot","summary_text":"Abstract-level arXiv Discovery lead (2608.21206) in lane evaluation. Discovery triage only: matched=evaluation,language_models,retrieval_embeddings,safety_security; title_matches=evaluation,language_models; score=10. Shortlist status is provisional and requires Sol review; no downstream disposition is encoded. Abstract excerpt: Person names are widely used as prompt variables in LLM evaluations of factuality, privacy leakage, bias and abstention, but when a name's evidential status is uncontrolled, measurements may conflate memorisation, retrieval, name priors and wrong-person attribution. We operationalise an unknown name as one with plausible First-Last form, no indexed full-name evidence, and no ambiguity signals under a documented validation run, and introduce PUN (Plausible Unknown Names), a protocol for constructing and validating such names, combining Wikidata-derived components, web-enabled LLM screening, and","title":"No PUN Intended: Plausible Unknown Names for Person-Centred LLM Evaluation"}}
